.TH WORDCOUNT 1 "September 2026" "OS Assignment 01" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
wordCount \- count lines, words and characters in a file

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B int wordCount(FILE *file, int *lines, int *words, int *chars);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The wordCount function reads a file and calculates the number of lines, words and characters. It returns 0 when the operation succeeds and -1 when an invalid argument or error occurs.

